  "title": "agentscan: test an x402 payment and get a signed receipt of what the gate saw (health ping)"
 },
 "description": "agentscan: Make a real x402 payment to test your wallet and client, with a signed receipt. To check a signed authorization without paying use x402_payment_status; to vet a seller before paying use check_x402_endpoint_before_paying. Returns what the payment gate saw, with an Ed25519-signed UTC receipt; a `sha256` you send is signed with the time, as a simple proof that it existed then. Built for a scheduled health ping: every call settles a new payment on-chain. A failed payment is never settled, and its 402 names the reason (wrong network, amount or payTo, expired or bad signature). The receipt key is at /.well-known/tanod-receipt-key. Typically 1-4 s (one on-chain settlement). Price: USD 0.001. No free tier. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/x402-payment-test-api.html",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "sha256": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
      "maxLength": 64,
      "minLength": 64,
      "type": "string"
     },
     {
      "type": "null"
     }
    ],
    "default": null,
    "description": "Optional: a SHA-256 hash as 64 hex characters. It is signed together with the time, as a simple proof that something with this hash existed then.",
    "title": "Sha256"
   }
  },
  "title": "test_x402_paymentArguments",
  "type": "object"
 },
